  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added tests to `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes: 13 tests, the 2 existing ones plus 11 new ones for `slugify`.\n\nHow it works, in order:\n1. It lowercases the text.\n2. It removes accents by splitting each accented letter into a base letter plus accent marks and dropping the marks. That covers Vietnamese (`Tiếng Việt` → `tieng-viet`) and other Latin text (`Crème Brûlée`, `São`).\n3. A few Latin letters have no accent to strip, so a small table maps them directly: `đ`/`Đ` → `d`, plus `ð`, `ł`, `ø`, `ı`, `ß`→`ss`, `æ`→`ae`, `œ`→`oe` and `þ`→`th`. The table goes beyond the rules you gave, so \"other Latin text\" also ends up as plain ASCII.\n4. Each run of characters that aren't a–z or 0–9 becomes one `-`, and hyphens at the start or end are removed.\n5. It cuts the result to 50 characters and then removes any trailing hyphen the cut left behind. The 50-character limit applies to the finished slug, not the input text.\n\nThe new tests cover:\n- lowercasing\n- Vietnamese and other accented letters, and `đ`/`Đ`\n- runs of symbols collapsing to one hyphen\n- trimming hyphens at either end\n- digits\n- empty or symbols-only input, which gives `''`\n- the 50-character limit\n- a cut that would otherwise end on a hyphen",
